lsmp-library: licence

Copyright (c) 2026 LSMP

1. LSMP's own material
   The collection files as assembled and annotated by LSMP, the puzzle selections, the hints,
   the sheet layouts, the puzzle data files, the README, AGENTS and index files, and this library as a whole are licensed under the
   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0):
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
   The full legal code is at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode
   You may copy, share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes if you give credit,
   link to the licence and indicate changes. Suggested credit:
   "lsmp-library, Copyright (c) 2026 LSMP, CC BY-NC 4.0".

2. Lichess puzzle data
   Puzzle positions, ids, ratings and themes come from the Lichess puzzle database
   (https://database.lichess.org/#puzzles), released under Creative Commons CC0 1.0 (public
   domain dedication). That data is free to use without conditions. It is credited in
   the credits, content/chess-com-collections/sources.md. The hints, selection and sheet design that LSMP added to it fall under clause 1.

3. Third-party material
   Games and annotations made by others (for example Lichess study authors and chess.com
   lesson authors), the typeface embedded in the PDF sheets, and the board and piece artwork
   in the PDF sheet diagrams are not LSMP's own material and are not covered by clause 1.
   They remain with their owners. Credits are in content/chess-com-collections/sources.md and, per game, in the PGN
   header tags (Source, Annotator, StudyName, ChapterURL, GameURL). Please keep them.

Pupils' names are deliberately absent from this library. Please do not try to restore them.
